PART 2 - FEMNIST (no drift telemetry; no correlation attempted)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Distinct writers: 2095 (10 campaign clients, 2085 held-out) | 472734 samples
Empirical global prior: min=0.00271 max=0.05511 (uniform = 0.01613); max/min ratio = 20.4x
Max deviation from uniform: 0.03898 | JS(global || uniform) = 0.15621

Ranking disagreement CV (uniform ref) vs JS (global ref)
  SCOPE: the aggregated pool of 2095 distinct writers - NOT the campaign's 10-client federation, which is analysed separately below.
  Spearman between the two rankings          : 0.6909
  Pool writers changing H_k tercile band     : 756/2095 (36.1%)
  Pool writers whose E_k would differ        : 504/2095 (24.1%)  [quantile matching; budget preserved GLOBALLY over the pool, not within any subset]

  Sensitivity of that pooled figure to how JS is placed on the CV scale:
    quantile_matching     24.1%  budget 9226 vs 9226 (preserved)
    min_max               54.7%  budget 10218 vs 9226 (INFLATED)
    raw_js                57.6%  budget 10400 vs 9226 (INFLATED)
    Only quantile matching isolates re-ranking; the others inflate the budget, conflating reordering with simply training more.

Most prior-like writer overall (lowest JS): f1447_28 JS=0.0167, CV=0.1394 (CV percentile 22.0)
Among the 5% most prior-like writers, the one the CV penalises most: f1136_31 JS=0.0379 (pct 3.9) vs CV=0.1535 (pct 37.4)
Most extreme case that actually changes the epoch budget:
  f3942_06: JS=0.0710 (percentile 28.1) but CV=0.1928 (percentile 63.8)
  n_k=182, classes covered=61/62, E_k(CV)=4 vs E_k(JS)=5

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PART 2b - COUNTERFACTUAL RANK REMAPPING WITHIN THE CAMPAIGN FEDERATION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Within-federation, budget-preserving rank remapping over the 10 writers the
campaign actually uses as clients, evaluated on all 30 seeds. The exact
multiset of E_k values assigned by the CV is preserved and redistributed by
the JS ranking. This is a counterfactual reallocation, NOT an algorithm:
it is not 'FedHAD-JS', nothing was trained, and it claims nothing about
accuracy or drift.

  Seeds evaluated                 : 30
  Budget preserved in every seed  : True  (total epochs before = after in 30/30 seeds)
  Total epochs per seed           : [43] (CV) vs [43] (remapped)
  Writers changing E_k per seed   : mean 3.6 of 10 (min 2, max 4)
  Spearman CV vs JS within the federation: mean 0.533 [0.224, 0.709]

  Transition matrix over 300 (writer, seed) pairs:
    E_k 4 -> 4 : 156  (unchanged)
    E_k 4 -> 5 :  54  (CHANGED)
    E_k 5 -> 4 :  54  (CHANGED)
    E_k 5 -> 5 :  36  (unchanged)

  Writers that change in at least one seed: 8 of 10
  Most frequently reallocated writers (seeds affected):
    f0900_42: 30/30 seeds
    f0150_25: 24/30 seeds
    f3844_11: 22/30 seeds
    f1702_13: 18/30 seeds
    f2402_75: 7/30 seeds

